<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1184" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aeglē</span></b> , ēs, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴγλη</span> (brightness). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A nymph</i>, <i>daughter of Jupiter
				and Neœra</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aegle Naïadum pulcherrima,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 6, 21</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of the Hesperides</i>, <i>daughter
				of Atlas</i>, <i><span class="en">Serv. ad Verg. A. 4,
			484</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A daughter of the Sun</i>, <i>sister
				of Phaëthon</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				154</span></i> and 156.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>